BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the general equations of motion for a rigid body of mass m in planar motion: translational equations Sigma Fx = m*a_Gx, Sigma Fy = m*a_Gy and rotational equation Sigma M_G = I_G*alpha.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Representation of a Rigid Body as a System of Particles:) Tj
T*
(   Consider a rigid body composed of an infinite continuum of differential mass elements dm_i.) Tj
T*
(   Let G be the center of mass with position vector r_G. Let r_i be the position vector of mass) Tj
T*
(   element dm_i) Tj
T*
(   relative to fixed origin O, and let r'_i be its position vector relative to G \(r_i = r_G +) Tj
T*
(   r'_i\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Derivation of Translational Equations of Motion:) Tj
T*
(   For each individual particle, Newton's Second Law gives: dF_i\(ext\) + dF_i\(int\) = dm_i * a_i.) Tj
T*
(   Summing over all particles: Sigma dF_i\(ext\) + Sigma dF_i\(int\) = Integral\(a_i dm\).) Tj
T*
(   By Newton's Third Law, internal action-reaction forces cancel identically in pairs: Sigma) Tj
T*
(   dF_i\(int\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   By definition of center of mass: m * r_G = Integral\(r_i dm\).) Tj
T*
(   Differentiating twice with respect to time:) Tj
T*
(   m * a_G = Integral\(a_i dm\)) Tj
T*
(   Therefore, we obtain the translational equations of motion:) Tj
T*
(   Sigma F = m * a_G ===> Sigma Fx = m * a_Gx, Sigma Fy = m * a_Gy. \(Q.E.D.\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Derivation of Rotational Equation of Motion about G:) Tj
T*
(   Take the moment of all forces about the center of mass G:) Tj
T*
(   Sigma M_G = Integral\( r'_i x a_i dm \)) Tj
T*
(   Since r_i = r_G + r'_i, acceleration is a_i = a_G + a'_i.) Tj
T*
(   Substitute: Sigma M_G = Integral\( r'_i x \(a_G + a'_i\) dm \) = [ Integral\(r'_i dm\) ] x a_G +) Tj
T*
(   Integral\( r'_i x a'_i dm \).) Tj
T*
(   By definition of centroid: Integral\(r'_i dm\) = 0.) Tj
T*
(   For planar motion in the x-y plane, relative acceleration is: a'_i = \(alpha x r'_i\) - omega^2 *) Tj
T*
(   r'_i.) Tj
T*
(   Taking cross product with r'_i:) Tj
T*
(   r'_i x a'_i = r'_i x \(alpha x r'_i\) = alpha * \(r'_i dot r'_i\) = \(r'_i\)^2 * alpha) Tj
T*
(   Therefore:) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
