12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Derive the linear acceleration a_G and minimum static friction coefficient mu_s required for pure rolling without slipping of a uniform solid cylinder of mass m and radius R down an incline of angle theta.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Problem Definition & Free Body Diagram \(FBD\):) Tj
T*
(   Solid circular cylinder: Mass m, radius R, centroidal mass MOI: I_G = 0.5 * m * R^2.) Tj
T*
(   Incline angle: theta to horizontal. Let coordinate x be directed down the incline.) Tj
T*
(   Forces acting on the rolling cylinder:) Tj
T*
(   - Gravity component down incline: W_x = m * g * sin\(theta\).) Tj
T*
(   - Gravity component normal to incline: W_y = m * g * cos\(theta\).) Tj
T*
(   - Normal reaction N perpendicular to incline \(upward\).) Tj
T*
(   - Friction force F_f acting up the incline at contact point C to resist slipping.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Kinematic Constraint for Pure Rolling Without Slipping:) Tj
T*
(   Contact point C is instantaneously at rest: a_C = 0 => a_G = R * alpha => alpha = a_G / R.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Dynamic Equations of Motion:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) Translational equation down the incline \(Sigma Fx = m * a_Gx\):) Tj
T*
(   m * g * sin\(theta\) - F_f = m * a_G ===> [Equation 1]) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) Normal force equilibrium \(Sigma Fy = 0\):) Tj
T*
(   N - m * g * cos\(theta\) = 0 => N = m * g * cos\(theta\) ===> [Equation 2]) Tj
T*
(   \(c\) Rotational equation about center of mass G \(Sigma M_G = I_G * alpha, clockwise +\):) Tj
T*
(   F_f * R = I_G * alpha) Tj
T*
(   Substitute I_G = 0.5 * m * R^2 and alpha = a_G / R:) Tj
T*
(   F_f * R = \(0.5 * m * R^2\) * \(a_G / R\) = 0.5 * m * R * a_G) Tj
T*
(   F_f = 0.5 * m * a_G ===> [Equation 3]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Solving for Acceleration a_G and Friction Force F_f:) Tj
T*
(   Substitute Equation 3 into Equation 1:) Tj
T*
(   m * g * sin\(theta\) - 0.5 * m * a_G = m * a_G) Tj
T*
(   1.5 * m * a_G = m * g * sin\(theta\)) Tj
T*
(   a_G = \(1 / 1.5\) * g * sin\(theta\) = \(2/3\) * g * sin\(theta\).) Tj
T*
(   Substitute a_G into Equation 3 for friction force:) Tj
T*
(   F_f = 0.5 * m * [ \(2/3\) * g * sin\(theta\) ] = \(1/3\) * m * g * sin\(theta\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Minimum Static Friction Coefficient mu_s:) Tj
T*
(   To prevent slipping, Coulomb friction requires: F_f <= mu_s * N.) Tj
T*
(   \(1/3\) * m * g * sin\(theta\) <= mu_s * [ m * g * cos\(theta\) ]) Tj
T*
(   mu_s >= \(1/3\) * [ sin\(theta\) / cos\(theta\) ] = \(1/3\) * tan\(theta\).) Tj
T*
(   Conclusion: a_G = \(2/3\)*g*sin\(theta\); mu_s_min = \(1/3\)*tan\(theta\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
