(   point O.) Tj
T*
(   Let G be the center of mass located at distance d below suspension point O \(OG = d\).) Tj
T*
(   Let I_G = m * k_G^2 be the centroidal mass moment of inertia, where k_G is radius of gyration.) Tj
T*
(   By the Parallel Axis Theorem, mass moment of inertia about pivot O is:) Tj
T*
(   I_O = I_G + m * d^2 = m * \(k_G^2 + d^2\)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Derivation of Differential Equation of Motion:) Tj
T*
(   Let theta be the angular displacement from the vertical position.) Tj
T*
(   Restoring gravitational torque about pivot O:) Tj
T*
(   M_O = - \(m * g\) * \(d * sin\(theta\)\)) Tj
T*
(   Applying the rotational equation of motion about fixed pin O \(Sigma M_O = I_O * alpha\):) Tj
T*
(   I_O * \(d^2theta / dt^2\) = - m * g * d * sin\(theta\)) Tj
T*
(   I_O * \(d^2theta / dt^2\) + m * g * d * sin\(theta\) = 0) Tj
T*
(   For small amplitude oscillations: sin\(theta\) =~ theta \(in radians\):) Tj
T*
(   \(d^2theta / dt^2\) + [ \(m * g * d\) / I_O ] * theta = 0) Tj
T*
(   Substitute I_O = m * \(k_G^2 + d^2\):) Tj
T*
(   \(d^2theta / dt^2\) + [ \(g * d\) / \(k_G^2 + d^2\) ] * theta = 0) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Natural Frequency and Time Period:) Tj
T*
(   This is standard Simple Harmonic Motion: \(d^2theta / dt^2\) + omega_n^2 * theta = 0.) Tj
T*
(   omega_n = sqrt\( \(g * d\) / \(k_G^2 + d^2\) \)) Tj
T*
(   Time Period T = 2 * pi / omega_n:) Tj
T*
(   T = 2 * pi * sqrt\( \(k_G^2 + d^2\) / \(g * d\) \)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Equivalent Length of Simple Pendulum \(L_eq\) and Centre of Percussion C:) Tj
T*
(   Comparing with a simple pendulum period T = 2*pi*sqrt\(L/g\):) Tj
T*
(   L_eq = \(k_G^2 + d^2\) / d = d + \(k_G^2 / d\)) Tj
T*
(   The point C located at distance L_eq from pivot O along line OG is the Centre of Oscillation /) Tj
T*
(   Percussion.) Tj
T*
(   Conjugate Property: If the body is inverted and suspended from point C, its distance to G is d') Tj
T*
(   = k_G^2 / d.) Tj
T*
(   The new period is T' = 2*pi*sqrt\(\(k_G^2 + d'^2\)/\(g*d'\)\) = 2*pi*sqrt\(L_eq/g\) = T! Suspension and) Tj
T*
(   percussion points are mutually interchangeable.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
