(   [Problem Statement]: A reciprocating slider-crank mechanism has a crank OA of length r = 150 mm rotating counterclockwise at constant speed N = 300 RPM. Connecting rod AB has length L = 500 mm. At theta = 60 deg with the horizontal stroke line, calculate: \(1\) Velocity of crank pin A, \(2\) Angular velocity of connecting rod AB, \(3\) Velocity of slider B.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Angular Speed and Velocity of Crank Pin A:) Tj
T*
(   Angular velocity of crank OA:) Tj
T*
(   omega_OA = 2 * pi * N / 60 = 2 * pi * 300 / 60 = 10 * pi = 31.416 rad/s.) Tj
T*
(   Velocity of crank pin A \(perpendicular to crank OA\):) Tj
T*
(   v_A = r * omega_OA = 0.150 m * 31.416 rad/s = 4.712 m/s.) Tj
T*
(   Direction of v_A: inclined at 60 + 90 = 150 deg to positive x-axis \(up and left\).) Tj
T*
(   Components: v_Ax = - 4.712 * sin\(60\) = - 4.081 m/s; v_Ay = + 4.712 * cos\(60\) = + 2.356 m/s.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Incline Angle beta of Connecting Rod AB:) Tj
T*
(   Applying the sine rule to triangle OAB:) Tj
T*
(   \(r / sin\(beta\)\) = \(L / sin\(60 deg\)\)) Tj
T*
(   sin\(beta\) = \(0.150 / 0.500\) * sin\(60 deg\) = 0.300 * 0.866025 = 0.2598) Tj
T*
(   beta = asin\(0.2598\) = 15.06 degrees; cos\(beta\) = cos\(15.06 deg\) = 0.9657.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Relative Velocity Analysis \(v_B = v_A + v_B/A\):) Tj
T*
