/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
45 780 Td
(   2. Dynamic Equation for the Suspended Beam:) Tj
T*
(   Applying Newton's Second Law vertically downward \(Sigma Fy = m * a\):) Tj
T*
(   W - T = m * a) Tj
T*
(   2452.5 - T = 250 * a ===> T = 2452.5 - 250 * a [Equation 1]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Rotational Equation for the Hoisting Drum:) Tj
T*
(   Cable tension T acts tangentially at radius R = 0.40 m to produce driving torque:) Tj
T*
(   Sigma M_O = I_O * alpha) Tj
T*
(   T * R = I_O * \(a / R\)) Tj
T*
(   T = \(I_O / R^2\) * a) Tj
T*
(   Substitute numerical values for drum inertia:) Tj
T*
(   I_O / R^2 = 13.50 / \(0.40\)^2 = 13.50 / 0.16 = 84.375 kg \(Equivalent drum inertia mass\).) Tj
T*
(   T = 84.375 * a [Equation 2]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Solving for Acceleration 'a' and Tension T:) Tj
T*
(   Equating Equation 1 and Equation 2:) Tj
T*
(   2452.5 - 250 * a = 84.375 * a) Tj
T*
(   \(250 + 84.375\) * a = 2452.5) Tj
T*
(   334.375 * a = 2452.5) Tj
T*
(   a = 2452.5 / 334.375 = 7.335 m/s^2.) Tj
T*
(   Substitute 'a' into Equation 2 to find cable tension T:) Tj
T*
(   T = 84.375 * 7.335 = 618.89 N.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Final Results:) Tj
T*
(   - Downward acceleration of the beam: a = 7.335 m/s^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Cable tension during descent: T = 618.89 N.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
