/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 10:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A uniform circular disk of mass m = 8 kg and radius R = 0.25 m is placed on a horizontal surface. A horizontal pulling force P = 40 N is applied at the center of the disk. If the surface is sufficiently rough to ensure pure rolling without slipping, calculate: \(1\) Linear acceleration of center of mass a_G, \(2\) Frictional force F_f acting at contact point, \(3\) Minimum coefficient of static friction mu_s.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Equations of Motion for the Pulled Rolling Disk:) Tj
T*
(   Mass: m = 8 kg; Radius: R = 0.25 m; Applied force: P = 40 N at center G.) Tj
T*
(   Centroidal MOI: I_G = 0.5 * m * R^2 = 0.5 * 8 * \(0.25\)^2 = 4 * 0.0625 = 0.25 kg-m^2.) Tj
T*
(   Let a_G be acceleration to the right, and alpha be angular acceleration \(clockwise\).) Tj
T*
(   Pure rolling constraint: a_G = R * alpha => alpha = a_G / R.) Tj
T*
(   Let F_f be friction force at contact point C \(assume pointing backward, to the left\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Formulation of Equations:) Tj
T*
(   \(a\) Horizontal translational equation \(Sigma Fx = m * a_G\):) Tj
T*
(   P - F_f = m * a_G ===> 40 - F_f = 8 * a_G [Equation 1]) Tj
T*
(   \(b\) Rotational equation about center of mass G \(Sigma M_G = I_G * alpha, clockwise +\):) Tj
T*
(   F_f * R = I_G * alpha = \(0.5 * m * R^2\) * \(a_G / R\) = 0.5 * m * R * a_G) Tj
T*
(   F_f = 0.5 * m * a_G = 0.5 * 8 * a_G = 4 * a_G [Equation 2]) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Simultaneous Solution:) Tj
T*
(   Substitute Equation 2 into Equation 1:) Tj
T*
(   40 - \(4 * a_G\) = 8 * a_G) Tj
T*
(   12 * a_G = 40) Tj
T*
(   a_G = 40 / 12 = 3.333 m/s^2.) Tj
T*
(   Substitute a_G into Equation 2 for friction force:) Tj
T*
(   F_f = 4 * 3.333 = 13.33 N \(directed to the left, opposing motion\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
endobj
